A||N||5||martin1875||3.4  starter||||4||
Z||000000||martin1875||12-17-2000||06:38 PM||||iam thinking about putting a 3.4 in my fiero, and was wondering why you have to move the starter to the other side of the block. sorry if this is a dumb question||||reg||4
Z||000001||fierosound||12-17-2000||06:49 PM||||Depends what the 3.4L came from.  Camaros are RWD (rear wheel drive) so their starters are mounted on the opposite side of the engine.  If you use a 3.4 from a GM car or van with FWD (front wheel drive) the starters are mounted the same as in the Fiero, as the Fiero setup is essentially a FWD powertrain.<P>I've just recently done a 3.4L swap myself.  there are more links at the forum below  <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/005508.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/005508.html</A> <P>More details at photos here  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/calgaryfieros/tonys87.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/calgaryfieros/tonys87.htm</A> <p>[This message has been edited by fierosound (edited 12-17-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||tgowens||12-17-2000||07:31 PM||||when installing a 3.4 RWD from a '93-'95 Camaro/Firebird (which IS the easiest swap) the starter must be moved to the other side of the block to allow the starter to turn the proper direction -- it involves drilling three mounting holes to reposition the starter. There are more considerations as well such as the airconditioner bracket, the front lower strut mount bracket, the wiring harness and ECM from a 2.8 as well as the plenum, intakes, manifolds, etc from the 2.8......<P>Hope this helps......||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfiero||12-17-2000||07:39 PM||||The main reason to relocate the starter is because it interferes with the axles in FWD applications (such as the Fiero).||||reg||1
Z||000004||martin1875||12-17-2000||07:55 PM||||thanks for the help i thought it would be in the way. is there a kit you can buy to drill your own starter hole, or can most machine shops perform the job||||reg||1
Z||000005||HYPTNOTiSE||12-18-2000||01:44 PM||||I dont know if Ed parks is closer to you, but you could come up one day and get your starter holes drilled at my place.  I'll drilland tap your starter holes for 100 dollars. <P>------------------<BR>       Mike LeCompte<BR>86 Fiero GT 3.2L w/ Nitrous<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.tcac.net/~daddyg/hypsig.gif"> ||||reg||1
